From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:30:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(opencode): resolve the channel-named database for resume
 and derive

`path resume --harness opencode` projected into `opencode.db`, but a
current opencode (1.18.18, channel `stable`) opens
`opencode-stable.db` and answered `Error: Session not found`. Decoded
from its bundle, opencode resolves `$OPENCODE_DB` first, then
`opencode.db` only on the latest/beta/prod channels or with
`$OPENCODE_DISABLE_CHANNEL_DB`, else `opencode-<channel>.db`; it never
migrates or reads the legacy file.

`PathResolver` now mirrors that: `$OPENCODE_DB` (or `with_db_file`)
pins the file; otherwise `db_candidates()` is `opencode-stable.db` then
`opencode.db`, and `db_path()` is the first that exists, or
`opencode-stable.db` when neither does. Resume therefore writes the
file the installed opencode reads and derive reads the one it shows;
the two files are deliberately not kept in sync. The rule and its two
version witnesses are documented in paths.rs and
docs/agents/formats/opencode.md.

Verified end to end in a hermetic HOME: project the codex golden with
the fixed binary, `opencode --session <id>` under understudy renders
the full history.
